  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing the probabilities of favorable outcomes and preferring the lottery with higher probability of such outcomes. In this case, Lottery B has a 100% probability of 2400 Euros, while Lottery A has a 99% probability of at least 2400 Euros (33% + 66%). Thus, Lottery B has a higher probability of achieving the favorable outcome of 2400 Euros. The individual’s deliberation focuses on the certainty of the outcome in B versus the probabilistic nature of A, and they explicitly justify their choice based on the security of the outcome. This aligns with the decision reason: the individual prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome (2400 Euros). The information considered (probabilities of favorable outcomes) and the justification (preference for higher probability of secure gain) match the decision reason's rule. Therefore, the individual used the reason to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

